<title>UK: Syria buys white and raw sugar for November -trade.</title>
<headline>Syria buys white and raw sugar for November -trade.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Syria bought 26,000 tonnes of sugar for November shipment dates, traders said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Syria's General Foreign Trade Organisation for Chemicals and Foodstuffs (GEZA) bought 13,000 tonnes of raw sugar from a European trade house at $312.94 per tonne, they said.</p>
<p>GEZA also bought 13,000 tonnes of white sugar at around $364 a tonne from a London-based house. --Jeremy Smith, London Newsroom +44 171 542 8064</p>
